    <briefdescription>
<para>Keeps a set of PHINodes. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a minimal set implementation for a specific use case: It is very fast when there are very few elements, but also provides good performance when there are many. It is similar to <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_small_ptr_set" kindref="compound">SmallPtrSet</ref>, but also provides iteration by insertion order, which is deterministic and stable across runs. It is also similar to <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_small_set_vector" kindref="compound">SmallSetVector</ref>, but provides removing elements in O(1) time. This is achieved by not actually removing the element from the underlying vector, so comes at the cost of using more memory, but that is fine, since PhiNodeSets are used as short lived objects. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
